{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011CggkkevyebQrGRmNHjqai","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"The high-spin to low-spin crossover happens at **Dq ≈ 1 958 cm⁻¹** (10Dq ≈ 19 580 cm⁻¹, Dq/B ≈ 2.12).\n\n**What changes at the crossover:** below this point the ground state is the high-spin ⁴T₁g(F) term, mostly t₂g⁵e_g². Above it, the low-spin ²E_g term, mostly t₂g⁶e_g¹, is the ground state.\n\n**How I found it:** I diagonalised the full d⁷ ligand-field Hamiltonian, covering all 120 Slater determinants, numerically.\n- The interelectron repulsion used the Slater–Condon parameters F₂ = 49B + 7C and F₄ = 441C/35 (in units with F₀ omitted), with B = 922 cm⁻¹ and C = 4 156 cm⁻¹.\n- The octahedral crystal field was added on top, as a function of Dq.\n- This includes all configuration interaction. That matters here, because ⁴T₁g(F) mixes with ⁴T₁g(P), and ²E_g mixes with doublets from other configurations. A simple pairing-energy estimate would miss both effects.\n\n**Checks on the calculation:**\n- The free-ion terms come out correctly: ⁴P lies 15B = 13 830 cm⁻¹ above ⁴F, and ²G lies 4B + 3C = 16 156 cm⁻¹ above ⁴F.\n- At Dq = 1 000 cm⁻¹, the ⁴T₂g level lies 8 776 cm⁻¹ above the ground state.\n\n**Locating the crossing:** I tracked the energy gap E(lowest doublet) − E(lowest quartet) as Dq increased:\n\n| Dq (cm⁻¹) | Gap (cm⁻¹) |\n|---|---|\n| 1 500 | +4 478 |\n| 1 800 | +1 548 |\n| 2 000 | −412 |\n\nRoot-finding puts the zero, where the ⁴T₁g and ²E_g levels are equal in energy, at Dq = 1 958 cm⁻¹. A Dq/B of about 2.1 is consistent with the d⁷ Tanabe–Sugano diagram for C/B ≈ 4.5.\n\n{\"Dq\": 1958, \"B\": 922, \"C\": 4156, \"out_of_scope\": false, \"reason\": \"Full d7 ligand-field diagonalisation gives the 4T1g/2Eg crossing at Dq ≈ 1958 cm^-1.\"}"}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":579,"cache_read_input_tokens":6